<header class="hero" id="home"><div class="hero-inner"><div class="eyebrow">HERITAGE Â· ARCHITECTURE Â· ENGINEERING</div><h1>FORTVISION<br><span>Exploring Maharashtraâ€™s Fort Heritage</span></h1><p>An academic and architectural exploration of Maharashtraâ€™s historic hill and sea fortresses â€” their ingenious water systems, defensive design, rugged basalt landscapes and enduring cultural legacy.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn" href="https://maharashtrasfort.netlify.app/#forts">EXPLORE THE FORTS&nbsp; â†—</a><a class="btn outline" href="https://maharashtrasfort.netlify.app/#knowledge">DISCOVER THE KNOWLEDGE</a></div><div class="stats"><div class="stat"><strong>350+</strong><small>Historic fortresses</small></div><div class="stat"><strong>12</strong><small>UNESCO-listed fort components</small></div><div class="stat"><strong>400+</strong><small>Years of engineering heritage</small></div><div class="stat"><strong>4</strong><small>Traditional knowledge themes</small></div></div></div></header>
<section id="about"><div class="intro-grid"><div><div class="section-head"><div class="kicker">Our purpose</div><h2>Heritage is more than history.</h2><p>This digital explorer presents forts as living examples of traditional Indian knowledge. Their design reflects careful observation of terrain, climate, materials, water availability and strategic needs. By studying these systems, we can understand how earlier communities adapted to challenging landscapes.</p></div><p class="sans" style="font-size:13px;line-height:1.8;color:#68766d">The project connects the past with the present through accessible information, interactive fort profiles and learning activities. It is designed for students, visitors and anyone curious about Maharashtraâ€™s cultural landscape.</p></div><div class="quote"><p>â€œA fort is not only a defence structure; it is a carefully planned relationship between people, land, water and nature.â€</p><small>THE IDEA BEHIND THIS DIGITAL EXPLORER</small></div></div></section>
